                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_424">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        University</orgName><p>Erased inscription in three lines on front
                        pastedown immediately above and ?in the same hand as the table of contents.
                        The use of reagent has prevented the inscription from being clearer under UV
                        than in ordinary light. It includes the words, in the second line,
                        'M[agist]ri [Gil]berti [Kym]er'. E. W. B. Nicolson read the inscription,
                        presumably using reagent, and note that the manuscript 'belonged to Kymer
                        and was given to the library of the University.'</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Henry Morgan, who gave it to Richard
